  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A body weighs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>49</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> on a spring balance at the north pole. What will be its weight recorded on the same weighing machine, if it is shifted to the equator?</p><p>[Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and radius of earth, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>.</mo></math>]</p>"
